---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | AcornOps"
  description="How the AcornOps website uses privacy-friendly analytics and which event categories it measures."
  pathname="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="legal shell">
    <header class="legal__header">
      <p class="legal__kicker">Privacy note</p>
      <h1>Useful signals, minimal data.</h1>
      <p>Last updated 17 July 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="legal__body">
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-overview">
        <h2 id="privacy-overview">Overview</h2>
        <p>AcornOps uses Plausible Analytics on the production marketing website to understand which pages and product paths are useful. The website does not use analytics cookies, advertising trackers, or session replay.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-events">
        <h2 id="privacy-events">What we measure</h2>
        <p>We may record aggregate page views and four limited event categories:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Clicks on demo and documentation calls to action, categorized by page location and destination.</li>
          <li>Navigation clicks, categorized by destination.</li>
          <li>Completion of the product walkthrough, categorized by target type.</li>
          <li>Views of the workspace overview, assistant answer, and expanded run-trace states.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The website adapter accepts only predefined property values. It does not send free-form text, full URLs, email addresses, user IDs, target identifiers, or other personal data in custom events.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-cookies">
        <h2 id="privacy-cookies">Cookies and identifiers</h2>
        <p>This site does not set an analytics cookie or use a persistent analytics identifier. A cookie banner is therefore not shown for the analytics configuration described here.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-links">
        <h2 id="privacy-links">External services</h2>
        <p>Links to the demo console, documentation, and GitHub open services with their own privacy practices. Following one of those links leaves this marketing website.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-contact">
        <h2 id="privacy-contact">Questions</h2>
        <p>For privacy questions or requests, open an issue in the <a href="https://github.com/acornops" data-track-navigation="github">AcornOps GitHub organization</a>. Do not include secrets, credentials, or sensitive personal information in a public issue.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>

  <script>
    import { initAnalytics } from '@/scripts/analytics';
    initAnalytics();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
